(BUF-41: `Release <buffer>.` and `Deallocate <buffer>.` are accepted as
 the same statement as `Free <buffer>.` — three interchangeable
 spellings, each emptying the buffer identically.
 Also covers: BUF-42 (all three accept an optional article `the`).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/usr/share/vox/coreasm /usr/bin/vox BUF-41.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   0
   0
   0
   0
   0
   0
)
a buffer called buf1 is "one".
a buffer called buf2 is "two".
a buffer called buf3 is "three".
Free buf1.
Release buf2.
Deallocate buf3.
print buf1's size.
print buf2's size.
print buf3's size.

a buffer called buf4 is "four".
Free the buf4.
print buf4's size.

a buffer called buf5 is "five".
Release the buf5.
print buf5's size.

a buffer called buf6 is "six".
Deallocate the buf6.
print buf6's size.
